# Create-file formats (CreateItemModal badges)

When adding a **new vault note/document extension** that users create via “새 파일” (e.g. `.enc.md`, `.slide.md`), register it in the **same change** so `CreateItemModal` shows a format badge. Do not hardcode badges in the modal.

## What counts

- User-creatable note/document file extensions offered in CreateItemModal
- Composite extensions that still open as markdown (or a related editor), e.g. `.enc.md`

## What does not count

- Binary / media uploads
- Sidecars not created via CreateItemModal (e.g. `.sync.pb`, chat day files)
- Internal temp / session-only names (`untitled.md`)

## Where to register

| Step | Path |
|------|------|
| Format entry | `src/utils/createFileFormats.ts` → `CREATE_FILE_FORMATS` |
| Path resolve | `src/utils/createItemPath.ts` uses `ensureCreateFileExtension` (longest match) |
| Modal badges | `CreateItemModal` maps `CREATE_FILE_FORMATS` — do **not** add a one-off badge |
| Open / save / tree / search | Wire the extension where content is loaded, written, or indexed |

## Checklist

1. Add `{ id, extension, label, description, default? }` to `CREATE_FILE_FORMATS` (longest extensions first in matching via helpers).
2. Confirm `resolveCreateItemPath` keeps names that already end with the new extension.
3. Implement open/save (and lock UI / index skip if encrypted or opaque).
4. Prefer **English** in new code comments if Korean Unicode might corrupt.

```text
❌ BAD — support `.enc.md` open/save only; CreateItemModal still only implies `.md`
❌ BAD — hardcode a second badge button inside CreateItemModal
✅ GOOD — one CREATE_FILE_FORMATS row; modal maps the list into badges
✅ GOOD — longest-match extension (`.enc.md` before `.md`)
```
